                <td width=572 valign=center colspan=10 style="width:343.6000pt;padding:0.0000pt 5.4000pt 0.0000pt 5.4000pt ;border-left:none;
mso-border-left-alt:none;border-right:1.0000pt solid windowtext;mso-border-right-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;
border-top:none;mso-border-top-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;border-bottom:1.0000pt solid windowtext;
mso-border-bottom-alt:0.5000pt solid windowtext;">
                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p>Obstetrics and Gynecology Nursing is a science that diagnoses and deals with women's reactions to existing and potential health problems of reproductive system and provides services for women's reproductive health, which is an important part of modern nursing. The subjects of this course include women with different reproductive health status at different stages of life, as well as related family members and social members. The main teaching contents include anatomy and physiology of female reproductive system, nursing care of women in normal pregnancy, childbirth and puerperium, nursing care of pregnancy complications and complications, nursing care of patients with inflammation of female reproductive system, nursing care of patients with tumors of female reproductive system, nursing care of patients with menstruation-related diseases, health care of women in different life cycles, and family planning guidance</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
